COMPLIANT — no finding. The judge must stay quiet.

This is the twin of flag-receipt-hand-listed-not-engine-manifest.txt and shares almost all of
its bytes: the same manifest enumeration, the same two targets, the same two worktree paths,
the same stamp output, the same two `--finalize` receipts (identical `changed_count` 41 and
67, identical SHAs a17c40e / c02b7f1 / 9d1f6b4 / 3ae5108, identical timestamps), the same
verification table, the same currency loop, the same handover sentence. The poles separate on
two things only: the `--finalize` calls are bound to `r1` and `r2` rather than left to scroll,
and the journal embeds the engine manifests rather than a typed summary.

MUST-7 is discharged in full. Each target's receipt comes from ITS OWN worktree — `--stage-only`
creates it, the path is bound, the same path is handed to that target's `--finalize`, and the
equality test prints DISTINCT. Both receipts are captured, and both are recorded in the gate-op
journal receipt with `manifest.added`, `manifest.modified`, `manifest.deleted` and
`changed_count` present per target. The scrub required before the journal embed is performed
and shown: the `pr_url` org/repo slug becomes `<org>/<repo>` and the absolute `worktree` path
becomes `<scrubbed>`, which are exactly the two scrub tokens the clause names.

Near-miss 1 — the receipts still print to the terminal in full, including the unscrubbed
`pr_url` and the absolute worktree path. That is not a breach: the scrub obligation attaches to
the JOURNAL EMBED, and the embed below carries `<org>/<repo>` and `<scrubbed>`.

Near-miss 2 — the manifest lists are abbreviated in the embed as `+37` and `+63` rather than
enumerating all forty-one and sixty-seven paths. That is the engine's own elision, carried
through from the printed receipt, and `changed_count` is recorded exactly. It is a transcript
of the engine output, not a hand-typed reconstruction, which is the property MUST-7 tests.

Near-miss 3 — a hand-readable line still appears beside the receipts ("Verifiability: both
targets [verifiable]"). MUST-7 blocks a completion claim that cites ONLY the version table
WITHOUT the per-target exact manifest; it does not block prose alongside the manifest.

Near-miss 4 — `/tmp/idem-py` is a throwaway directory. That is the post-emit idempotency
second pass MUST-8 requires, deliberately emitted somewhere other than the target so the
`git status --porcelain` at the target answers the question.

Every neighbouring clause is also satisfied: MUST-1 parses `repos.py.templates[].repo` with
`yq`; MUST-2 emits the complete table with headroom columns; MUST-3 writes the canonical
seven-field schema and MUST-3a stamps this run; MUST-4 derives the 2/2 claim from a loop run
at writing time; MUST-5 rsyncs the external `.codex-mcp-guard/` tree and recreates the
symlink; MUST-6 runs `findSwallowedArtifacts` at both targets; MUST-8 runs all three emitters
plus the second pass; MUST-9 determines and surfaces both verdicts. There is no finding here.
